{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DisjointSet","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each set’s representative is one of its members. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"union(a, b)"},{"text":" keeps the representative of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the larger set, or, for sets of the same size, the smaller of the two representatives, whatever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order of the arguments. Neither ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find"},{"text":" nor a union of elements already in one set changes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a representative, so representatives depend only on the sequence of unions that merged sets.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two disjoint sets are equal when they have the same elements, partitioned the same way. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representative "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find"},{"type":"text","text":" returns is not part of the value: equal disjoint sets can name the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set by different representatives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is one array of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" integers, copied on write. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"union(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mutating"},{"type":"text","text":" because they shorten paths. Every other query works on a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"let"},{"type":"text","text":" and walks at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌊log₂ count⌋ steps, since union by size bounds the height."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/disjointsetmodule\/disjointset"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/init()","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/init(count:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/count","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/isEmpty","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/setCount"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/find(_:)","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/inSameSet(_:_:)","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/labels()","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/makeSet()","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/reserveCapacity(_:)","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/setSize(of:)","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/sets()","doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/union(_:_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DisjointSetModule\/documentation\/DisjointSetModule\/DisjointSet\/CustomDe